{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a9f3ce8333b3f8d7","name":"Viper-Series Probe Droid Battalion","source":{"id":"source:reference-a9f3ce8333b3f8d7","title":"Viper-Series Probe Droid Battalion","revision":18595,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:23:12Z","sha256":"3e70f26a5bae990b6dd15d5a145bcb1b4878467edad459ab2703a84eac9f8290","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18595","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Viper-Series%20Probe%20Droid%20Battalion&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a9f3ce8333b3f8d7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Before the rise of the Empire, Probe Droids- often referred to as probots- were used primarily to map space lanes, survey planets, and perform search-and-rescue operations. However, such friendly purposes fell by the wayside as the Emperor conquered more and more systems. Probots became tools for rooting out traitors on far-flung worlds. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arakyd Industries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arakyd_Industries","referenceId":"reference:53475569f2ae9d67"}," manufactures the Empire's favored model, the Viper-Series, for this very purpose.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Equipped with an extensive sensor system, the Viper is either deployed directly from the ground or fitted with an optional delivery system that guides the probot from a ship to the designated planet. The delivery system possesses only rudimentary breaking capacities, so it includes buffers to prevent damage to the Droid on impact. These are especially important, since the Imperial Viper's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Self-Destruct System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Self-Destruct_System","referenceId":"reference:69d3c9eb720267d8"}," is designed to destroy the Probe Droid if it takes significant damage (to prevent it from falling into enemy hands). The sub-light delivery system costs an additional 5,000 credits; a hyperspace-capable version sells for 15,000 credits.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Viper-Series Probe Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Viper-Series_Probe_Droid","referenceId":"reference:80ebc1ca754e6229"}," Battalion Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"},") ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["